## 2. Audit Trail Integrity & Independent Chain Reconstruction
The audit subsystem utilizes a strict cryptographic hash chaining mechanism (`SHA-256`) to guarantee log immutability:
* **Tamper Detection:** Every audit entry contains the cryptographic hash of the preceding entry (`prev_hash`), forming an unbroken chain[span_4](start_span)[span_4](end_span).
* **Independent Reconstruction:** In the event of log inspection or forensic analysis, the chain can be independently recomputed and verified from the genesis block. Any deletion, reordering, or modification of historical events invalidates all subsequent hashes, triggering an immediate security flag[span_5](start_span)[span_5](end_span).

